---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';

const WINDOW = '20 September – 31 October 2026';
const ROWS = [
	['Closed trades', '14 (12 counted, 2 excluded)'],
	['Winners / losers', '6 / 6'],
	['Win rate', '42.9%'],
	['Return', '+0.16% (+$15.72)'],
	['Profit factor', '1.40'],
	['Sharpe / Sortino', '0.21 / 0.40'],
	['Max drawdown', '−0.25%'],
	['Best / worst trade', '+4.06% / −2.60%'],
	['Inference cost', '$6.44 (8.8M in / 4.2M out tokens)'],
	['Net after inference', '+$9.28'],
	['Analyses', '83 cycles · median 277 s · $0.0125 each'],
];
const TRADES = [
	['24 Sep', 'LONG', '−2.60%', 'closed'],
	['24 Sep', 'LONG', '−2.06%', 'stop loss'],
	['28 Sep', 'LONG', '−0.28%', 'closed'],
	['02 Oct', 'LONG', '−0.99%', 'closed'],
	['05 Oct', 'LONG', '−1.12%', 'stop loss'],
	['10 Oct', 'SHORT', '+3.45%', 'take profit'],
	['12 Oct', 'SHORT', '+2.04%', 'take profit'],
	['14 Oct', 'SHORT', '+0.07%', 'stop loss'],
	['15 Oct', 'SHORT', '—', 'excluded (fill divergence)'],
	['17 Oct', 'SHORT', '—', 'excluded (fill divergence)'],
	['26 Oct', 'SHORT', '+1.93%', 'take profit'],
	['29 Oct', 'SHORT', '+2.25%', 'closed'],
	['30 Oct', 'LONG', '−1.11%', 'closed'],
];
---

<ArticleLayout
	title="Results — paper trading ledger | Semantic Signal"
	description="Paper-trading ledger for Semantic Signal: 14 closed BTC/USDC trades (12 counted), +0.16% against a −4.64% buy-and-hold, $6.44 of inference cost, and every caveat that belongs with those numbers."
	meta="Results"
>
	<span slot="title">Results, as the bot recorded them</span>
	<p slot="subtitle" class="subtitle">
		{WINDOW} · BTC/USDC · 4h candles · 10 000 USDC simulated capital · paper book with a testnet executor.
	</p>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>The ledger</h2>
		<p>
			Every number on this page is read from the bot's own runtime files (<code>statistics.json</code>,
			<code>api_costs.json</code>, <code>trade_history.db</code>, <code>metrics/cycles.jsonl</code>) plus one
			public Binance klines request for the benchmark. Nothing is typed from memory:
			<code>python scripts/results_report.py</code> prints it, and the
			<a href="https://github.com/qrak/LLM_trader#results" target="_blank" rel="noopener">README results table</a>
			quotes the same window.
		</p>

		<table class="ledger">
			<tbody>
				{ROWS.map(([label, value]) => (
					<tr><th>{label}</th><td>{value}</td></tr>
				))}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Versus holding the coin</h2>
		<p>
			Over the same 42 days the underlying went from <strong>81 245.48</strong> to
			<strong>77 473.56</strong> — a <strong>−4.64%</strong> buy-and-hold (only closed 4h bars).
			The bot finished <strong>+0.16%</strong>.
		</p>
		<figure class="chart">
			<img src="/results-vs-btc.png" width="1200" height="520" alt="Bot +0.16% versus BTC buy-and-hold −4.64% over the same window" loading="lazy" />
			<figcaption>Same window, same instrument. Four and a half points over six weeks is not an edge.</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Closed trades</h2>
		<p>
			One row per post-mortem the bot wrote. Thirteen rows cover thirteen of the fourteen closed trades:
			one was closed without a post-mortem row, so the ledger counts it and this table does not.
		</p>
		<table class="trades">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Closed</th><th>Side</th><th>P&amp;L</th><th>Exit</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{TRADES.map(([when, side, pnl, exit]) => (
					<tr>
						<td>{when}</td>
						<td>{side}</td>
						<td class={pnl.startsWith('+') ? 'up' : pnl.startsWith('−') ? 'down' : ''}>{pnl}</td>
						<td>{exit}</td>
					</tr>
				))}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Caveats</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Twelve counted trades cannot separate skill from noise.</strong> The sample is too small to read as a track record.</li>
			<li><strong>Fees are configured but not booked.</strong> The paper book records <code>fee = 0.0</code> (or no fee at all) on its rows, so the +$15.72 is gross of trading costs; at the configured 0.075% per side it would mostly disappear. See <a href="/articles/measurement/">where the numbers come from</a>.</li>
			<li><strong>Two trades are excluded on purpose</strong> — both sandbox exits printed below the real market low in the same minute, so they stay in execution history but not in statistics or in the brain's learning.</li>
			<li><strong>This is a paper book.</strong> The executor can reach an exchange testnet, not live funds.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Methodology, per-trade table and the reproduction command:
			<a href="https://github.com/qrak/LLM_trader/blob/master/README.md#results" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the README results section</a>.
			Watch the next cycle live on the <a href="https://semanticsignal.qrak.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dashboard</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
	.ledger,
	.trades {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		margin: 1.25rem 0;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}
	.ledger th,
	.ledger td,
	.trades th,
	.trades td {
		padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.18);
		text-align: left;
	}
	.ledger th {
		color: var(--muted, #94a3b8);
		font-weight: 500;
		width: 45%;
	}
	.trades th {
		color: var(--muted, #94a3b8);
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	}
	.up {
		color: #34d399;
	}
	.down {
		color: #f87171;
	}
	.chart {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
	}
	.chart img {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.16);
	}
	.chart figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.6rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--muted, #94a3b8);
	}
</style>
